```suggestion
    /// Return true if there is at least one task associated with this index
```

I am not sure I understand the problem.
If someone specifies `indexUid=catto`, then we'll hit line 495:
```rust
        if let Some(index) = &query.index_uid {
            let mut index_tasks = RoaringBitmap::new();
            for index in index {
                index_tasks |= self.index_tasks(rtxn, index)?;
            }
            tasks &= &index_tasks;
        }
```
and the taskDeletion, taskCancelation, etc. won't be returned.

If there is a `indexSwap(A, B)` and the API key only allows me to access A, then we'll hit line 605:
```rust
      // Any task that is internally associated with a non-authorized index
        // must be discarded.
        if let Some(authorized_indexes) = authorized_indexes {
            let all_indexes_iter = self.index_tasks.iter(rtxn)?;
            for result in all_indexes_iter {
                let (index, index_tasks) = result?;
                if !authorized_indexes.contains(&index.to_owned()) {
                    tasks -= index_tasks;
                }
            }
        }
```
which will remove the task from the results as well. (In the loop there, `index == B` and `authorised_indexes == [A]`, so `[A].contains(B)` will return false and we'll run `tasks -= [indexSwap(A,B)]`)
